Appendix C

Strengthened Dependent Type System and Soundness

We refine the type system of Chapter 5 to include the injectivity condition necessary for sound fault‑tolerance guarantees.

Definition C.1 (Code type). For natural numbers $n,k,d$,

\operatorname{\texttt{Code}}(n,k,d) := \{ (C_\bullet, \pi) \mid C_\bullet\in\mathbf{2QEC},\, \pi: (\dim C_0=n)\land(\dim H_1(C)=k)\land(\operatorname{dist}(C)\ge d) \}.
\]  

Definition C.2 (Morphism type). For $Q,R$ of type $\operatorname{\texttt{Code}}$, define

\begin{aligned}
\operatorname{\texttt{Morph}}(Q,R) := \{ f\in\operatorname{Hom}_{\mathbf{2QEC}}(C_Q,C_R) \mid &
(k_Q \le k_R) \;\land\; (d_Q \le d_R)\\
& \land\; (f_*: H_1(C_Q)\hookrightarrow H_1(C_R)) \\
& \land\; (f \text{ preserves the symplectic form on homology}) \}.
\end{aligned}
\]  

The last two conditions are encapsulated as explicit proof terms.

Typing rules.

· (Id) $\vdash \mathrm{id}_Q : \operatorname{\texttt{Morph}}(Q,Q)$.
· (Comp) If $\vdash f: \operatorname{\texttt{Morph}}(Q,R)$ and $\vdash g: \operatorname{\texttt{Morph}}(R,S)$, then $\vdash g\circ f : \operatorname{\texttt{Morph}}(Q,S)$.
· (Conv) If $\vdash f: \operatorname{\texttt{Morph}}(Q,R)$ and $\eta:f\Rightarrow g$ is a 2‑cell in $\mathbf{2QEC}$, then $\vdash g: \operatorname{\texttt{Morph}}(Q,R)$.

Theorem C.3 (Soundness). Any well‑typed morphism $f:\operatorname{\texttt{Morph}}(Q,R)$ satisfies $k_Q\le k_R$ and $d_Q\le d_R$, and the underlying chain map induces an injective map on homology, thereby preserving logical qubits. Hence a fault‑tolerant logical operation implementing $f$ can be composed.

Proof. By induction on the derivation. The base case (Id) is trivial. For composition, the inequalities and injectivity compose. For conversion, chain homotopy preserves homology maps, so injectivity is preserved. The distance inequality is part of the type and remains valid. ∎

This formulation eliminates the earlier gap: distance preservation is not derived from the morphism but is an explicit condition that must be supplied and checked.

